<title>USA: Samsonite prices offering at $42/shr.</title>
<headline>Samsonite prices offering at $42/shr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsonite Corp said on Thursday it priced its share offering at $42 per share.</p>
<p>The Denver-based company filed in December to offer 7.8 million shares. Thomas Sandler, the chief financial officer, said Samsonite sold a total of about 8.6 million shares including the &quot;green shoe,&quot; or over-allotment option by the underwriters.</p>
<p>Samsonite shares were up two at 44-3/4 in heavy volume on Nasdaq.  </p>
<p>Also, PaineWebber initiated coverage of the company's stock, which was one of the ten most actively traded issues, with a buy recommendation.</p>
